enu expands in the left navigation displaying its sub-items. Search Intransits page loads; Intransit grid is displayed with filter fields and default records. A random Transit ID value is captured from the data grid Transit ID column and stored for later use. Captured Transit ID value is entered in the transitId input filter field. Search button is clicked; grid refreshes and is filtered using the entered Transit ID. Assertion passes: every value in the Transit ID column of the filtered grid matches the captured Transit ID. A random Source Location value is captured from the data grid Source Location column and stored for later use. Captured Source Location is selected in the sourceLoc dropdown filter field. Search button is clicked; grid refreshes and is filtered using the selected Source Location. Assertion passes: every value in the Source Location column of the filtered grid matches the captured Source Location. A random BOL value is captured from the data grid BOL column and stored for later use. Captured BOL value is entered in the bolFilter text field. Search button is clicked; grid refreshes and is filtered using the entered BOL. Assertion passes: every value in the BOL column of the filtered grid matches the captured BOL. A random Project Name value is captured from the data grid Project Name column and stored for later use. Captured Project Name is entered in the projectName text filter field. Search button is clicked; grid refreshes and is filtered using the entered Project Name. Assertion passes: every value in the Project Name column of the filtered grid matches the captured Project Name. A random Shipping Carrier Name value is captured from the data grid shippingCarrierName column and stored for later use. Captured Shipping Carrier Name is entered in the CarrierNumberFilter text field. Search button is clicked; grid refreshes and is filtered using the entered Carrier Number/Name. Assertion passes: every value in the CarrierNumberFilter column of the filtered grid matches the captured Carrier Number/Name.','["url: https://ims.sws.pipe-piling.com/auth/ims/login","username: Puneet","password: ofbiz"]','2026-04-23 07:30:02','2026-08-27 04:39:00',1,'P1','["functional", "boundary", "regression"]',1,0),
(37741,NULL,103,1104,5502,'Optimized','STC_15 Verify Warehouse transfer creation and edit','["1. Launch and navigate to the IMS login page using url","2. Enter the valid username and password in their respective field","3. Click on the ‘Login’ button","4.  Click on Intransit button from left nav ","5. Click on Search Intransits button from left nav","6. Click on Warehouse Transfer button","7. Fill autocomplete from Location field information with From Location","8. Select PPMTL from auto suggestions from locations","9. Fill autocomplete to Location field information with To Location","10. Select ECLIPS from auto suggestions to location","11. Fill Beams in Product Type","12. Select auto suggestions from product type","13. Wait for 2 second and click on Search button","14. Capture the first product on where Stock on S/O (PCS) = 0 and Actual Yard Stock (PCS) > 1 and Net Available Stock for Sale (PCS) > 1","15. Click on Captured product checkbox","16. Click on title Add Products button","17. Click on \\"Create Bulk Intransit\\" button","18. Wait for 2 seconds","19. Assert: Verify \\"\\"Close Intransit\\"\\" button is visible \\"","20. Click on Edit button","21. Increase Qty To Transfer by 1 in gridcell","22. Wait for 10 seconds","23. Click on Save button","24. Wait for 5 seconds","25. Assert: Verify success message \\"Transaction completed successfully.\\""]','IMS login page loads successfully in the browser with Username field, Password field, and Login button visible. Username and password are accepted in their fields; password is masked with dots/asterisks. No validation errors appear. User is authenticated and redirected to the Home page; left navigation menu and header are displayed; session is established. Intransit section/menu expands in the left navigation displaying its sub-items. Search Intransits page loads; Intransit grid/list is displayed with toolbar (Warehouse Transfer button, filters, etc.) and default records. Warehouse Transfer creation screen opens with the "Warehouse Transfer" caption visible at the top left and required fields (From Location, To Location, product search, etc.) displayed. From Location autocomplete field is populated with the entered value (PPMTL); matching suggestions appear in the popper. From Location "PPMTL" is selected from the base-Popper-root suggestion list and reflected in the autocomplete-fromLocation field. To Location autocomplete field is populated with the entered value (ECLIPS); matching suggestions appear in the popper. To Location "ECLIPS" is selected from the base-Popper-root suggestion list and reflected in the autocomplete-toLocation field. Product search dialog/modal opens for the Enter Product Id field with filter controls visible. Product Type "Beam" is selected in the product search dialog; filter is applied to the search criteria. After a 2-second wait, the Search button is clicked; product grid loads with results matching the selected Product Type. First product where Stock on S/O (PCS) = 0 AND Actual Yard Stock (PCS) > 1 AND Net Available Stock for Sale (PCS) > 1 is identified and captured (product details stored for later use). Checkbox of the captured product is selected (checked state = true). Add Products button is clicked; the captured product is added to the Warehouse Transfer line items; product search modal closes and user returns to the Warehouse Transfer screen. "Create Bulk Intransit" button is clicked; bulk intransit creation is triggered; processing indicator/success message is shown and the page transitions to the created intransit view. 2-second wait completes; UI is fully loaded with the newly created intransit details. Assertion passes: the "Close Intransit" button is visible on the page (confirming the intransit was created successfully). Edit button is clicked; the intransit/line-item enters edit mode with editable fields (including Qty To Transfer) enabled. Qty To Transfer cell is incremented by 1 in the gridcell; updated value is reflected in the cell. 10-second wait completes; UI/back-end processing is complete and the updated value is committed to the gridcell. Save button is clicked; changes are persisted; save request is submitted successfully. 5-second wait completes; UI is updated with the saved state and any success notifications are visible. Assertion passes: the success message "Transaction completed successfully." is displayed on the screen.','["url: https://ims.sws.pipe-piling.com/auth/ims/login","username: Puneet","password: ofbiz","From Location: PPMTL","To Location: ECLIPS","Product Type: Beam"]','2026-04-23 07:30:02','2026-08-27 04:38:51',1,'P1','["functional", "boundary", "validation"]',1,0),
(37742,NULL,103,1104,5502,'Optimized','DSTC_18 Verify the close item button under the action button on edit screen.','["1. Launch and navigate to the IMS login page using url","2. Enter the valid username and password in their respective field","3. Click on the ‘Login’ button","4. Click on Order button from left nav ","5. Go to order.","6. Click on create new order tab.","7. Click on find with Bill to field.","8. Select an customer and click on + icon.","9. Enter customer id in \'Bill to\' field and click on check mark.","10. Verify Billing address.","11. Verify Ship to address.","12. Add the items and click on save button.","13.Select the item.","14.Click on action button and select the close item."]','1. IMS login page loads successfully in the browser with Username field, Password field, and Login button visible.   2. Username and password are accepted in their fields; password is masked with dots/asterisks. No validation errors appear.  3. User is authenticated and redirected to the Home page. Left navigation menu, header are displayed. 4. Order page loads; Order grid/list is displayed with toolbar (Create New Order button, filters, etc.).  5.After click on close item the item status should come (C). 6.After clicking on close item the system should show the pop up on screen(Do you want to close the item) and clicking on yes should mark the item status as close. 7.Order notes should also update.','["url: https://ims.sws.pipe-piling.com/auth/ims/login","username: Puneet","password: ofbiz","Supplier Party Id: ABD Boats","shipping carrier: CHA100 - CHALLENGER LOGISTICS","carrier BOL: B636363","url-part: dashboard/shipment","qtyValue: 1","invoicecomment: Test shipment to invoice"]','2026-04-23 07:30:02','2026-08-27 04:38:24',1,'P1','["functional", "edge-case", "validation"]',1,0),
