(37744,NULL,103,1104,5503,'Optimized','RTC_129 Validate Welding BOM cancellation and inventory update','["1. Launch and navigate to the IMS login page using url","2. Enter valid username","3. Enter valid password","4. Click on the ‘Login’ button","5. Click on Expand button in left MuiBox","6. Click on Inventory","7. Click on Welding BOM","8. Assert: Verify Welding BOM text is displayed","9. Click create welding BOM","10. Enter valid SO","11. Select Product type as PIPE","12. Select Location as PPMTL","13. Click search icon beside product to join","14. Enter OD Range From","15. Enter OD Range To","16. Enter WallT Range From","17. Enter WallT Range To","18. Click Search","19. Assert: The visible row count is ≥ 1","20. Select two pipe from the list where Actual Yard Stock>=1 and Stock on S/O=0 and capture there inventory details","21. Click Add Products","22. Enter Project Quantity as 5","23. Click on Save","24. Click on OK button on the popup","25. Capture BOM","26. Click on Cancel BOM button","27. Click on left navigation Report","28. Click on Inventory history report","29. Search Product Id","30. Verify Product information"]','IMS login page displays with Username and Password fields Username is successfully entered in the Username field Password is successfully entered and masked in the Password field User is authenticated and redirected to the IMS dashboard Left navigation panel expands to show all menu options Inventory module opens and displays available inventory options Welding BOM page displays "Welding BOM" title/header is clearly visible on the page Create Welding BOM form opens with all required input fields Sales Order (SO) number is entered successfully in the SO field "PIPE" is selected in the Product type dropdown "PPMTL" is selected in the Location dropdown Product search/filter dialog opens with filter criteria fields OD Range From value is entered successfully OD Range To value is entered successfully Wall Thickness Range From value is entered successfully Wall Thickness Range To value is entered successfully Search executes and product results populate the list At least 1 product row is displayed in the search results Two pipes matching the criteria are selected; inventory details (Product ID, Actual Yard Stock, Stock on S/O, OD, Wall Thickness) are captured Selected pipes are added to the Welding BOM items list Project Quantity field displays "5" BOM data is validated and saved to the system Success message popup closes; Welding BOM is created and displays confirmation Welding BOM details (BOM ID, items, quantities) are captured User is redirected to the Welding BOM list page Report menu expands or navigates to Reports section Inventory history report page displays with search and filter options Product history records display for the searched Product ID Captured product information matches the data displayed in the Inventory history report','["url: https://ims.sws.pipe-piling.com/auth/ims/login","username: Puneet","password: ofbiz"]','2026-04-23 07:30:02','2026-08-06 06:47:54',1,'P1','["functional", "regression", "validation"]',1,0),
(37745,NULL,103,1104,5503,'Optimized','Verify bulk save working on Order edit','["1. Launch and navigate to the IMS login page using url","2. Enter the valid username and password in their respective field","3. Click on the ‘Login’ button","4. Click on Order button from left nav ","5. Pick any existing Sales Order with more than 4-5 items.","6. Click on edit  order.","7. Update qty, Price, Price UOM, Description, hold item, Heat#, add new item.","8. Click on bulk save button."]','1. IMS login page loads successfully in the browser with Username field, Password field, and Login button visible.   2. Username and password are accepted in their fields; password is masked with dots/asterisks. No validation errors appear.  3. User is authenticated and redirected to the Home page. Left navigation menu, header are displayed. 4. Order page loads; Order grid/list is displayed with toolbar (Create New Order button, filters, etc.).  5. Grid should not refresh with every change on item level. 6. User should be able to make all the changes in one go by clicking on bulk save. 7. All the changes done by user before hitting bulk save should be updated on screen and pdfs on Order.','["url: https://ims.sws.pipe-piling.com/auth/ims/login","username: Puneet","password: ofbiz","Supplier Party Id: ABD Boats","shipping carrier: CHA100 - CHALLENGER LOGISTICS","carrier BOL: B636363","url-part: dashboard/shipment","qtyValue: 1","invoicecomment: Test shipment to invoice"]','2026-04-23 07:30:03','2026-06-03 13:14:16',1,'P1','["functional", "regression", "state-transition"]',1,0),
